>
  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="cost">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How much does a bathroom installation cost in St Helens?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A full new bathroom in St Helens starts from £4,995, supplied and fitted, including VAT. A bath to shower conversion starts from £2,395.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Job</th><th>Price, inc VAT</th><th>Typical time</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Cloakroom or WC</strong></td><td>from £2,495</td><td>A few days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Bath to shower conversion</strong></td><td>from £2,395</td><td>2 to 3 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>En-suite or shower room</strong></td><td>from £4,495</td><td>Set out in your quote</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Full bathroom, supplied and fitted</strong></td><td>from £4,995</td><td>5 to 10 working days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Labour-only full refit (your own suite)</strong></td><td>from £2,750</td><td>5 to 10 working days</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Moving a bathroom upstairs</strong></td><td>Priced at the free visit</td><td>Set out in your quote</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>What changes the price in St Helens?</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Moving the room.</strong> A bathroom moved upstairs needs a new waste route and new pipes.</li>
        <li><strong>Old cast iron.</strong> Corroded waste pipes in older terraces are best replaced.</li>
        <li><strong>The suite and tiles you pick.</strong> Premium ranges cost more.</li>
        <li><strong>Room size.</strong> More wall and floor means more tiling.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We spot these at the free visit, so they are in your price from the start. Only need a new shower? See our <a href="/showers-liverpool">shower installation</a> prices, from £375 fitted.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="included">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What is included in a St Helens bathroom installation?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Everything from the strip-out to the final clean. Your quote lists what is in and what is not.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Strip-out and disposal.</strong> The old suite and tiles leave with us. No skip needed.</li>
        <li><strong>All plumbing.</strong> New hot, cold and waste pipes to every fitting.</li>
        <li><strong>Tiling.</strong> James's team does the tiling, with the wet areas waterproofed first. Or we fit wall panels if you prefer.</li>
        <li><strong>The suite.</strong> Bath or shower, toilet, basin, taps and valves, fitted and sealed.</li>
        <li><strong>Electrics.</strong> Lights, extractor fans and shower circuits by our partner firm <a href="https://www.idealelectricalsolutions.co.uk">Ideal Electrical Solutions</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Making good.</strong> We test every joint, seal everything and clean before we leave.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You can buy your own tiles or suite. If you supply the suite, the labour-only price is from £2,750.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="move">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Can you move a downstairs bathroom upstairs in St Helens?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. We move ground floor bathrooms in WA10 terraces up to a bedroom, and price the whole job as one fixed sum.</p>
      <p>Many Victorian terraces in WA10 have the bathroom downstairs at the back. It was the old outside toilet and washroom. It was turned into a bathroom when indoor plumbing came in.</p>
      <p>That made sense then. But it uses up space you could have as a utility, a dining area or a garden room. More and more St Helens owners are moving the bathroom upstairs and taking that space back.</p>
      <h3>What the job involves</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>A new soil and waste route for the upstairs room</li>
        <li>New hot and cold pipes to the new position</li>
        <li>A full new bathroom, plumbed and tiled</li>
        <li>Capping off and making good in the old room</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We look at both rooms at the free visit. You then get one written price for the whole job, not a run of extras.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="how">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How long does a bathroom installation take in St Helens?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">A full bathroom usually takes 5 to 10 working days. A bath to shower conversion takes 2 to 3 days.</p>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Free home visit (about 45 minutes).</strong> We measure up and check the pipes, waste and walls. For a move, we look at both rooms.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed written price.</strong> The full spec, written down. What is included is listed, and so is what is not.</li>
        <li><strong>Day 1: strip-out.</strong> The old bathroom comes out and leaves with us.</li>
        <li><strong>Days 1 to 3: first fix.</strong> New pipes and waste go in. Our partner electricians do any wiring. If we find rot or a leak, we show you and price it first.</li>
        <li><strong>Days 3 to 7: walls and floor.</strong> Boarding, waterproofing and tiling, or wall panels.</li>
        <li><strong>Final days: fit and hand over.</strong> The suite goes in. We test every joint, seal it all and clean the room.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Moving a bathroom, bigger rooms or a lot of tiling take longer. Your quote gives you the dates.</p>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Want a price for your St Helens bathroom?</strong> Book a free home visit. No pressure to book.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="terraces">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What should I know about bathrooms in WA10 terraces?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Older St Helens terraces have solid brick walls and old cast iron waste. We plan for both before we start.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>Solid walls.</strong> We rarely chase pipes into them. We run pipes in neat boxing instead.</li>
        <li><strong>Odd pipe routes.</strong> Pipes often run where the bathroom was added, not where they should. We plan new routes at the visit.</li>
        <li><strong>Cast iron waste.</strong> Often corroded. We include replacing it in your fixed price.</li>
        <li><strong>Condensation.</strong> Solid walls get damp and mouldy without a good fan. Our partner electricians fit one as part of the job.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Back additions and rear extensions each have their own waste routes. We check and price yours at the visit, not after the strip-out.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="which">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Which option is right for me?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Start with what is wrong with the room now. If only the bath is the problem, a conversion may be all you need.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Bath to shower, from £2,395</h3>
          <p>Best if you rarely use the bath, or getting in and out is hard. Done in 2 to 3 days.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Full bathroom, from £4,995</h3>
          <p>Best if the suite, tiles and pipes are all tired. The whole room is new.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Move the bathroom upstairs</h3>
          <p>Best if the bathroom is in the downstairs extension and you want the space back. Priced at the visit.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Cloakroom or WC, from £2,495</h3>
          <p>A toilet and basin downstairs. Handy if you move the main bathroom up.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;"><strong>Not sure?</strong> We will tell you honestly at the free visit, even if the cheaper option is the right one.</p>
      <h3 id="landlords">Are you a St Helens landlord?</h3>
      <p>We refit bathrooms in rental homes and book the work into the gap between tenants. Many landlords own terraces in WA9 and WA10. Some add a second shower room for a shared house. Others replace a tired suite before the next tenant moves in.</p>
      <p>Wall panels are often a good pick for rentals. They are quick to fit and have no grout to clean. Tell us your void dates and we will plan around them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="postcodes">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Do you cover all St Helens WA postcodes?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. We fit bathrooms across St Helens and the towns around it.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Places and postcodes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>Central St Helens</strong></td><td>St Helens WA10, Fingerpost WA10, Eccleston WA10, Parr WA9, Thatto Heath WA9</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>North and east</strong></td><td>Haydock WA11, Rainford WA11, Billinge WA11, Newton-le-Willows WA12</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Towards Liverpool</strong></td><td>Prescot L34, Whiston L35, Rainhill L35</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Travel is included in your quote, wherever you are.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="why">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Why choose us as your St Helens bathroom fitters?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">One team for plumbing and tiling, a fixed price in writing, and a 12-month guarantee on our work.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <figure class="sg-photo">
          <picture>
            <source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/jobs/bathroom-bath-shower-fitted-480.webp 480w, /images/jobs/bathroom-bath-shower-fitted-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 400px" />
            <img src="/images/jobs/bathroom-bath-shower-fitted-960.jpg" alt="New bath and shower fitted by our bathroom team" width="960" height="1280" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </picture>
          <figcaption>A real job: new bath and shower fitted.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="sg-photo">
          <picture>
            <source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/jobs/shower-room-fitted-480.webp 480w, /images/jobs/shower-room-fitted-960.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 400px" />
            <img src="/images/jobs/shower-room-fitted-960.jpg" alt="Shower room fitted by our team" width="960" height="1280" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </picture>
          <figcaption>A real job: shower room fitted.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li><strong>One team.</strong> Plumbing and tiling by James's team. No gap while you wait for a tiler.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed price in writing.</strong> If we find something behind the old bath, we price it before we touch it.</li>
        <li><strong>We know St Helens homes.</strong> Rear extensions, solid walls and cast iron waste are checked at the visit.</li>
        <li><strong>Guaranteed.</strong> 12 months on our work, and £2 million public liability insurance.</li>
        <li><strong>Tidy.</strong> We clean up and take all the rubbish away with us.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
